Gabriel. Gabriel, listen to me.

228
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,867
<i> Listen to Mommy, okay?</i>

229
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:14,900
<i> Shh.</i>

230
00:12:15,367 --> 00:12:16,600
<i> Just stay here.</i>

231
00:12:16,733 --> 00:12:18,700
<i> Don't go anywhere, okay?</i>

232
00:12:18,833 --> 00:12:20,033
<i> Mommy loves you so much.</i>

233
00:12:20,167 --> 00:12:22,500
<i>No matter what happens,
always stay good.</i>

234
00:12:22,633 --> 00:12:25,300
<i>Don't forget everything
I taught you, okay?</i>

235
00:12:25,433 --> 00:12:27,000
[CRYING] Okay, Mommy.

236
00:12:27,133 --> 00:12:29,200
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:12:29,333 --> 00:12:30,800
[CRYING] Mommy.

238
00:12:30,933 --> 00:12:32,600
[BELINDA] I love you so much.

239
00:12:34,967 --> 00:12:37,400
- [YOUNG GABO CRYING]
- [BELINDA SHUSHING]

240
00:12:37,533 --> 00:12:42,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:12:42,733 --> 00:12:44,500
<i>- Just stay here. Hide here.
- Mommy.</i>

242
00:12:44,633 --> 00:12:47,567
<i>Don't follow me, okay?
Just stay here.</i>

243
00:12:49,767 --> 00:12:52,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

244
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,133
<i> Ricardo!</i>

245
00:12:56,133 --> 00:12:58,433
<i>Ricardo, have mercy
on my family.</i>

246
00:12:58,567 --> 00:13:00,533
<i> Take me instead. Take me.</i>

247
00:13:00,667 --> 00:13:02,333
<i> Please don't hurt them.</i>

248
00:13:02,467 --> 00:13:03,633
<i> Ricardo, please.</i>

249
00:13:03,767 --> 00:13:06,533
<i>- Aah!
- Damn you!</i>

250
00:13:08,867 --> 00:13:09,767
[BELINDA WHIMPERS]

251
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:12,433
[CRYING] Mommy!

252
00:13:12,567 --> 00:13:13,567
[WHIMPERS] Ricardo.

253
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:17,833
<i>I can't believe you chose
that dirt-poor Rudy!</i>

254
00:13:17,967 --> 00:13:19,533
[YOUNG RICARDO
GRUNTS IN ANGER]

255
00:13:19,667 --> 00:13:21,233
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [BELINDA GROANS]

256
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,700
[CRYING]

257
00:13:23,733 --> 00:13:25,167
<i> Ricardo, please.</i>

258
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:26,667
<i> I'm begging you.</i>

259
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,200
<i> Ricardo, have mercy on us.</i>

260
00:13:28,333 --> 00:13:30,867
[BELINDA CRYING]
<i> Please, I'm begging you.</i>

261
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:34,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

262
00:13:34,933 --> 00:13:35,867
- [GUNSHOT]
- [CRYING]

263
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,567
[GABO] I saw how Mama died.

264
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:40,500
<i> Those bastards!</i>

265
00:13:40,633 --> 00:13:44,967
<i>I won't stop until I get
justice for Mama's death.</i>

266
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:45,967
[MUFFLED SOBS]

267
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:53,067
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

268
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:55,667
[MAN] Sir! Sir!

269
00:13:56,733 --> 00:13:58,500
<i> We found the gold!</i>

270
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:03,800
<i> Sir, let's go.</i>

271
00:14:04,733 --> 00:14:05,733
<i> Sir.</i>

272
00:14:07,733 --> 00:14:12,200
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:14:12,333 --> 00:14:14,700
[MUSIC FADES]

274
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:18,833
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

275
00:14:18,967 --> 00:14:21,000
<i> Mommy.</i>

276
00:14:26,633 --> 00:14:27,833
<i> Belinda.</i>

277
00:14:30,367 --> 00:14:31,767
<i> Belinda.</i>

278
00:14:34,267 --> 00:14:41,233
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [YOUNG GABO CRYING]

279
00:14:55,767 --> 00:15:02,733
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [YOUNG RUDY CRYING]

280
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:06,300
- [YOUNG GABO]<i> Mommy.
</i>- [YOUNG RUDY] Sorry.

281
00:15:07,933 --> 00:15:10,200
<i> Love, I'm-- I'm so sorry.</i>

282
00:15:10,333 --> 00:15:11,967
<i> Please forgive me, love.</i>

283
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:14,900
[YOUNG GABO AND YOUNG
RUDY CRYING]

284
00:15:15,033 --> 00:15:16,500
<i> I'm sorry.</i>

285
00:15:16,633 --> 00:15:23,633
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

286
00:15:24,633 --> 00:15:27,667
[YOUNG GABO CRYING]

287
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:29,567
[YOUNG GABO] Mommy.

288
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:33,500
[YOUNG GABO AND YOUNG
RUDY CRYING]

289
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:40,600
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:15:42,833 --> 00:15:44,100
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> From now on...</i>

291
00:15:45,033 --> 00:15:47,500
<i> it's just the two of us.</i>

292
00:15:47,633 --> 00:15:49,433
<i> But don't worry, son.</i>

293
00:15:49,567 --> 00:15:51,900
<i> I will never abandon you.</i>

294
00:15:52,033 --> 00:15:54,200
<i>I won't allow the two of us
to be separated.</i>

295
00:15:54,333 --> 00:15:55,600
<i> Don't forget that, okay?</i>

296
00:15:55,733 --> 00:16:02,633
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

297
00:16:04,567 --> 00:16:10,400
[YOUNG GABO CRYING]

298
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:14,433
[YOUNG GABO] Bye, Mommy.

299
00:16:14,567 --> 00:16:19,667
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

300
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,233
That gold...

301
00:16:22,967 --> 00:16:26,633
is the reason
we lost everything.

302
00:16:26,767 --> 00:16:32,567
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

303
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,367
Is it because
of that cop, Pa?

304
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:38,367
Is it because of that cop
who killed my mother?

305
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,100
Gabo...

306
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:44,100
It's best that you
don't know.

307
00:16:44,233 --> 00:16:46,600
You're on the right
path now.

308
00:16:46,733 --> 00:16:50,200
Don't be tempted
to do something wrong.

309
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:55,000
I made a lot of mistakes
in the past.

310
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:59,400
But I know that
I raised you well.

311
00:16:59,533 --> 00:17:01,700
You have a good heart, Gabo.

312
00:17:01,833 --> 00:17:03,767
You're not like me.

313
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:05,667
Pa...

314
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:09,067
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

315
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:11,600
I need to find that cop.

316
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:15,267
He has to pay
for what he did to my mother.

317
00:17:16,967 --> 00:17:18,700
And what he did to you.

318
00:17:20,167 --> 00:17:22,800
He's the reason
we are suffering today.

319
00:17:24,033 --> 00:17:26,033
I need to find him!

320
00:17:26,167 --> 00:17:27,500
Ga--Gabo.

321
00:17:27,633 --> 00:17:28,633
Gabo!

322
00:17:28,767 --> 00:17:35,700
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

323
00:17:41,233 --> 00:17:47,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

324
00:17:50,033 --> 00:17:51,167
[ISOBEL] Ricardo.

325
00:17:52,467 --> 00:17:54,433
Can we talk about Sam?

326
00:17:54,433 --> 00:17:55,500
[MUG CLATTERS]

327
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:58,267
[SIGHS] Okay.
What about Sam?

328
00:17:58,267 --> 00:18:02,233
Our daughter grew up smart.

329
00:18:02,233 --> 00:18:07,067
As parents, we're here
to guide, not dictate her.

330
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:09,933
What's wrong
with you, Isobel?

331
00:18:09,933 --> 00:18:11,700
Why are you
always defending her?

332
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:14,533
Her disobedience
in the workplace protocol

333
00:18:14,533 --> 00:18:18,100
only shows that she lacks
discipline and respect

334
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:19,667
to those superior to her.

335
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:23,633
[ISOBEL] She doesn't mean
to disrespect you,

336
00:18:23,667 --> 00:18:26,567
dishonor you, to hurt you.

337
00:18:26,567 --> 00:18:30,233
She's actually protecting
your name!

338
00:18:30,233 --> 00:18:31,967
Well, that's not how I see it,

339
00:18:31,967 --> 00:18:35,333
[ISOBEL] Because you're being
so close-minded.

340
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,400
You always snap at her!

341
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:38,800
Me?

342
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:40,133
Close-minded?

343
00:18:40,133 --> 00:18:46,200
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,533
[MAX] So,
are you enjoying this?

345
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:52,267
Your parents are arguing
first thing in the morning.

346
00:18:53,367 --> 00:18:54,533
Of course not.

347
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:58,067
Yes, because this is the result
of your stubbornness.

348
00:18:58,700 --> 00:19:01,400
I already handled the problem.

349
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,133
I just didn't know--

350
00:19:03,133 --> 00:19:04,567
That you would get caught?

351
00:19:04,933 --> 00:19:07,233
Sam, are you not thinking?
That's our father!

352
00:19:07,233 --> 00:19:10,267
If you listened to him when
he told you to lie low,

353
00:19:10,267 --> 00:19:12,500
they wouldn't
be arguing like this.

354
00:19:13,733 --> 00:19:16,867
Isobel, our children were born
into a policeman's family.

355
00:19:17,733 --> 00:19:19,267
To a General!

356
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:22,533
My reputation is not ordinary,

357
00:19:22,533 --> 00:19:25,000
so my demands for them
to protect my name

358
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,533
isn't ordinary either!

359
00:19:26,533 --> 00:19:33,533
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

360
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:38,100
[SIGHS]

361
00:19:41,767 --> 00:19:42,967
[SIGHS]

362
00:19:46,933 --> 00:19:48,833
- Mommy?
- Oh, Sam.

363
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,267
I'm sorry.

364
00:19:54,433 --> 00:19:56,767
You're arguing about me again.

365
00:19:56,767 --> 00:19:58,200
What? No.

366
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:00,400
Your father has a lot in mind.

367
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:04,933
I think it's because they're
hosting a party for Generals.

368
00:20:06,033 --> 00:20:08,033
Don't worry about it.
It's okay.

369
00:20:09,833 --> 00:20:10,967
Mom.

370
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:12,967
You're always defending him.

371
00:20:13,567 --> 00:20:14,967
And you always defend me.

372
00:20:16,833 --> 00:20:21,667
Maybe it's time we should be
responsible with our actions.

373
00:20:22,667 --> 00:20:23,800
Especially me.

374
00:20:24,633 --> 00:20:27,267
That was just the only way
I could think of

375
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:30,033
so that everything
wouldn't get worse.

376
00:20:33,967 --> 00:20:35,267
Mom, I'm sorry.

377
00:20:36,267 --> 00:20:41,300
I'll fix all the problems
I've caused.

378
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:42,400
I'll fix it.

379
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:44,567
I believe you can, Sam.

380
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:51,500
I need to go, mom.

381
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:58,500
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

382
00:21:04,033 --> 00:21:06,467
[SIGHS]

383
00:21:12,067 --> 00:21:13,367
[DJANGO] Hey.

384
00:21:14,067 --> 00:21:16,433
Par queen straight.
Full ace.

385
00:21:16,433 --> 00:21:17,667
[MAN] I lost.

386
00:21:17,667 --> 00:21:19,400
- [LAUGHTER]
- Isn't that Django?

387
00:21:19,400 --> 00:21:21,867
- [ROMY] Why is he still here?
- Oh, I'm so happy.

388
00:21:21,867 --> 00:21:23,867
- [DJANGO LAUGHS]
- [PAQUITO] Django.

389
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,933
Shouldn't you guys
be leaving already?

390
00:21:26,933 --> 00:21:30,167
Aren't you supposed to ambush
the reporter today?

391
00:21:30,167 --> 00:21:31,000
Pa.

392
00:21:31,767 --> 00:21:33,100
That's already taken care of.

393
00:21:34,267 --> 00:21:37,900
Django, every move
we make is important.

394
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:41,067
We could lose everything if
you make even just one mistake.

395
00:21:42,833 --> 00:21:46,567
Pa, I already
handled it last night.

396
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:48,233
Relax.

397
00:21:48,767 --> 00:21:49,867
[PAQUITO] As you should!

398
00:21:50,467 --> 00:21:55,467
If we mess up this job that
Umali is making us do,

399
00:21:55,467 --> 00:21:57,567
we're going to lose
a lot of money!

400
00:21:58,167 --> 00:21:59,533
So do a good job!

401
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:03,700
Go! Get a move on!

402
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:08,367
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

403
00:22:08,367 --> 00:22:10,000
- Hey!
- Boss.

404
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,533
Get a move on it.
Now!

405
00:22:14,033 --> 00:22:15,633
These two
are the bad influence.

406
00:22:20,167 --> 00:22:21,500
- [CASTOR] Sir.
- [SEBASTIAN] Hmm?

407
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:22,867
What's the update?

408
00:22:22,867 --> 00:22:25,433
Mr. Chan refuses to talk.

409
00:22:25,433 --> 00:22:28,767
He won't speak because
you never saw any gold.

410
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:33,333
If it is proven that his
arrest was unauthorized

411
00:22:33,333 --> 00:22:34,833
will the NCIA be held liable?

412
00:22:34,833 --> 00:22:36,333
Nope. It's just you.

413
00:22:36,333 --> 00:22:37,933
- Just us?
- Yeah.

414
00:22:37,933 --> 00:22:40,133
Wow.
Thanks for the support.

415
00:22:40,133 --> 00:22:41,967
Your operation was illegal.

416
00:22:41,967 --> 00:22:43,467
There was no order
from the higher-ups.

417
00:22:43,467 --> 00:22:45,933
For your information,
Ernesto,

418
00:22:45,933 --> 00:22:47,833
we just supported Ma'am Sam.

419
00:22:47,833 --> 00:22:48,267
I know that.

420
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:49,067
I know that.

421
00:22:49,067 --> 00:22:50,900
[KAREN] And we don't regret it.

422
00:22:50,900 --> 00:22:53,133
Karen, why are you here?

423
00:22:53,133 --> 00:22:55,900
- Is your wound healed?
- I feel restless at home.

424
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:57,900
I can't stop thinking
about Mr. Chan's case.

425
00:22:58,567 --> 00:23:02,233
Guys, if Mr. Chan talks
to his lawyer,

426
00:23:02,233 --> 00:23:05,000
he may file
a claim against you.

427
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:08,367
You had no warrant
when you arrested him.

428
00:23:08,367 --> 00:23:10,867
He could also file
an administrative case.

429
00:23:10,867 --> 00:23:14,400
Unless he cooperates with us.

430
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:17,733
He admits that he has
connections with Victor Zafra,

431
00:23:17,733 --> 00:23:19,800
and if he points out
where the gold is.

432
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:24,567
If that happens, then
your actions have a legal basis.

433
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:26,700
If that's the case, then fine.

434
00:23:27,367 --> 00:23:29,067
I'll make him confess.

435
00:23:29,067 --> 00:23:33,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

436
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:36,900
Sam, Sir Delgado
already warned you.

437
00:23:37,767 --> 00:23:38,867
Ma'am.

438
00:23:38,867 --> 00:23:40,800
Don't add
to your violations anymore.

439
00:23:40,800 --> 00:23:42,700
We'll just prove to him

440
00:23:42,700 --> 00:23:45,067
that catching
Mr. Chan wasn't a mistake.

441
00:23:45,067 --> 00:23:48,433
If he needs to tell everything
he knows about Zafra,

442
00:23:48,433 --> 00:23:49,633
then he'll do it.

443
00:23:51,167 --> 00:23:52,400
Sam, hold on.

444
00:23:53,367 --> 00:23:54,533
[CLEARS THROAT]

445
00:23:54,533 --> 00:23:55,967
You can't stop me.

446
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,167
I know.
That's why I'm going with you.

447
00:23:59,133 --> 00:24:00,167
Let's go.

448
00:24:00,167 --> 00:24:07,133
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

449
00:24:10,367 --> 00:24:13,100
[APPLAUDING]

450
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:14,567
You're very good.

451
00:24:15,333 --> 00:24:16,933
You pretended to be a buyer.

452
00:24:17,867 --> 00:24:19,333
You fooled me.

453
00:24:20,233 --> 00:24:21,633
Look at you.

454
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:24,267
- Look at me.
- [CUFFS RATTLING]

455
00:24:26,533 --> 00:24:28,233
How are you connected
to Victor Zafra?

456
00:24:29,700 --> 00:24:31,200
What do you know about him?

457
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,300
He's in jail, right?

458
00:24:34,733 --> 00:24:36,000
[CHUCKLES]

459
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,967
You'll end up with him
if you don't tell the truth.

460
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:40,800
Are you part of his group?

461
00:24:42,533 --> 00:24:44,267
Where's the gold you have?

462
00:24:45,933 --> 00:24:49,533
I will not tell you.

463
00:24:49,533 --> 00:24:51,100
I don't know.

464
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:55,267
Those guys you fought
at the warehouse,

465
00:24:55,267 --> 00:24:57,300
they were Victor Zafra's men,
weren't they?

466
00:24:58,300 --> 00:25:00,333
Your life is in danger.

467
00:25:02,100 --> 00:25:06,133
Listen, you don't know
who you're messing with.

468
00:25:06,467 --> 00:25:08,667
The Zafras are killers.

469
00:25:09,267 --> 00:25:11,500
They will kill you!

470
00:25:11,500 --> 00:25:12,833
[LAUGHS]

471
00:25:12,833 --> 00:25:14,500
I'm not scared of them!

472
00:25:14,500 --> 00:25:16,033
[LAUGHS]

473
00:25:17,033 --> 00:25:19,133
[BORROMEO] Ma'am Sam
shouldn't have

474
00:25:19,133 --> 00:25:20,800
interrogated Mr. Chan just yet.

475
00:25:22,267 --> 00:25:26,467
I don't know if Sam is
determined or just stubborn.

476
00:25:26,467 --> 00:25:28,933
[RALLOS] The review about her
on Mr. Chan's case

477
00:25:28,933 --> 00:25:30,700
isn't even finished yet,
and here she goes again.

478
00:25:30,700 --> 00:25:31,933
You know how Sam is.

479
00:25:31,933 --> 00:25:34,867
She won't stop if she's
focused on it.

480
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:37,100
But right now,
she has too many violations.

481
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:40,633
I hope she gets something
out of Mr. Chan.

482
00:25:40,633 --> 00:25:44,867
If not, then she's screwed
to Sir Delgado and Ma'am Pia.

483
00:25:45,867 --> 00:25:48,167
[MR. CHAN] I will not talk.

484
00:25:48,167 --> 00:25:53,633
[LAUGHS]

485
00:25:53,633 --> 00:25:56,100
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

486
00:25:58,200 --> 00:26:00,733
Sir, here's the decision of the
Internal Affairs Department

487
00:26:01,633 --> 00:26:03,367
regarding Jacinto's case.

488
00:26:04,867 --> 00:26:08,067
Considering her service record,

489
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:13,133
is there a chance for her
to have a lighter sanction?

490
00:26:13,300 --> 00:26:15,267
Based on our investigation,

491
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:18,233
that is the appropriate
disciplinary action.

492
00:26:18,367 --> 00:26:19,633
Okay. Thank you very much.

493
00:26:19,767 --> 00:26:21,400
- Excuse me, sir.
- Mm.

494
00:26:26,067 --> 00:26:27,300
- Sir?
- Yes?

495
00:26:27,433 --> 00:26:28,500
[DOOR CLOSES]

496
00:26:28,633 --> 00:26:31,733
Do you know what your favorite
agent is doing right now?

497
00:26:31,867 --> 00:26:32,900
Who?

498
00:26:33,033 --> 00:26:34,333
Samantha!

499
00:26:35,933 --> 00:26:38,333
She's in the
interrogation room right now...

500
00:26:38,467 --> 00:26:41,033
...with Mr. Chan.

501
00:26:41,167 --> 00:26:42,300
What?!

502
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:44,633
- I don't know!
- I know that you know...

503
00:26:44,767 --> 00:26:47,600
...that your life is in danger
with Victor Zafra!

504
00:26:47,733 --> 00:26:49,067
Do you understand that?

505
00:26:50,167 --> 00:26:51,733
[SAM] How about this?
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

506
00:26:51,867 --> 00:26:53,200
Give us information

507
00:26:53,333 --> 00:26:55,100
and we'll give you
witness protection.

508
00:26:55,233 --> 00:26:58,367
Yeah, fess up and cooperate.

509
00:26:58,500 --> 00:27:00,633
[SAM] We can even
lighten your sentence.

510
00:27:00,767 --> 00:27:03,533
Just fess up
and we'll help you.

511
00:27:05,467 --> 00:27:11,200
You will use my word against me
to get out of trouble?

512
00:27:11,333 --> 00:27:14,133
You are very desperate already.

513
00:27:14,267 --> 00:27:15,367
B****!

514
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,633
When I'm asking you,
you better answer properly!

515
00:27:20,500 --> 00:27:21,267
Well?!

516
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:24,033
You are not a good agent!

517
00:27:24,167 --> 00:27:26,667
You are careless and worthless!

518
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:27,833
[SPITS]

519
00:27:30,333 --> 00:27:31,667
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

520
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:37,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

521
00:27:37,567 --> 00:27:39,233
You--
Don't stop me!

522
00:27:39,367 --> 00:27:40,733
You bastard!

523
00:27:40,867 --> 00:27:42,667
- Jacinto!
- She hit me!

524
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:45,100
She hit me here! She hit me!

525
00:27:45,233 --> 00:27:47,567
Sir, he was rude!
I was talking to him nicely--

526
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:50,767
- To my office! Now!
- She hit me! She hit me! Help!

527
00:27:50,933 --> 00:27:57,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

528
00:28:05,667 --> 00:28:09,900
[MAMENG] Good thing the doctors
agreed to let Rudy go home

529
00:28:10,033 --> 00:28:12,133
and continue his recovery there.

530
00:28:12,867 --> 00:28:14,833
Oh. Hey, Gabo.

531
00:28:14,967 --> 00:28:17,433
Doctors said we can
take your father home.

532
00:28:18,967 --> 00:28:22,833
Nothing's really impossible
by the grace of God.

533
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:27,367
Rudy, the doctors agreed
to let us take you home.

534
00:28:27,500 --> 00:28:31,400
They just said to make sure
you take your prescribed meds.

535
00:28:31,533 --> 00:28:32,767
Where's Gabo?

536
00:28:32,900 --> 00:28:34,600
He's sitting outside.

537
00:28:35,500 --> 00:28:40,833
You know, supposedly, a problem
was waiting for you at home.

538
00:28:40,967 --> 00:28:41,900
What is it?

539
00:28:42,033 --> 00:28:43,833
You know that bike?

540
00:28:43,967 --> 00:28:46,900
The one that's owned
by a seaman?

541
00:28:47,033 --> 00:28:49,433
Your son messed with it.

542
00:28:49,567 --> 00:28:52,633
He almost lost it.
Good thing he got it back.

543
00:28:55,133 --> 00:28:57,733
Since he got it back,
just let it slide.

544
00:28:57,900 --> 00:28:58,800
Huh?

545
00:28:58,933 --> 00:29:00,833
Well, what are we waiting for?

546
00:29:01,967 --> 00:29:04,267
- Are you ready to go?
- Yeah, we're ready.

547
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:06,133
- Let's go?
- I'll help you change.

548
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:09,800
[GABRIEL]<i> I grew up yearning
</i> for a mother.

549
00:29:09,933 --> 00:29:11,533
- [BELINDA]<i> Gabriel, listen.
</i>- [YOUNG GABO CRYING]

550
00:29:11,667 --> 00:29:14,367
<i>Listen to Mommy, okay?
Mommy loves you so much.</i>

551
00:29:14,500 --> 00:29:16,833
<i>No matter what happens,
be kind, okay?</i>

552
00:29:16,967 --> 00:29:19,567
<i>Remember everything
I taught you.</i>

553
00:29:19,700 --> 00:29:21,333
[YOUNG GABO CRYING]
<i> Yes, Mommy.</i>

554
00:29:21,467 --> 00:29:23,567
[GABO]<i> I grew up
</i> feeling something was missing

555
00:29:23,700 --> 00:29:25,767
<i>because I lost my mother
as a child.</i>

556
00:29:25,900 --> 00:29:28,000
<i> Mommy!</i>

557
00:29:28,133 --> 00:29:29,333
[GABO] And to this day,

558
00:29:29,500 --> 00:29:32,700
<i>we haven't received justice
for what they did to my mother.</i>

559
00:29:32,833 --> 00:29:36,867
<i>Those cops caused me
so much suffering.</i>

560
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:39,933
<i>I'll make sure
to find out who they are.</i>

561
00:29:40,067 --> 00:29:41,733
<i> I'll hunt them down</i>

562
00:29:41,867 --> 00:29:44,433
<i>and get back at them
for my mother.</i>

563
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:48,033
<i> I'll make their families feel</i>

564
00:29:48,167 --> 00:29:52,833
<i>the same pain and agony
I suffered for years.</i>

565
00:29:52,967 --> 00:29:55,033
<i> I'll kill them all</i>

566
00:29:55,167 --> 00:29:58,200
<i>and I will not spare
their families.</i>

567
00:29:59,633 --> 00:30:03,000
<i>Admin put you
under preventive suspension.</i>

568
00:30:03,167 --> 00:30:04,667
<i> Well-deserved!</i>

569
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:06,267
<i>I just did
what I thought was right.</i>

570
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:09,533
<i> You did what you wanted.</i>

571
00:30:09,667 --> 00:30:11,567
<i>What? Are you going
to hit me, too?</i>

572
00:30:11,700 --> 00:30:13,633
<i>I'm not going to sit here
and do nothing</i>

573
00:30:13,767 --> 00:30:15,267
<i>while Samantha Jacinto
is out there.</i>

574
00:30:15,400 --> 00:30:16,633
<i> I'll make her pay, Ma!</i>

575
00:30:16,767 --> 00:30:18,533
<i>- You know what to do.
- I won't fight back!</i>

576
00:30:18,667 --> 00:30:20,067
I want you to make it spotless.

577
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:21,900
<i>If you fail,
I'll put you all down.</i>

578
00:30:22,033 --> 00:30:23,900
<i>Isn't Gabo supposed to
be with you? Where is he?</i>

579
00:30:24,033 --> 00:30:25,833
<i>He's not yet here?
He left before us.</i>

580
00:30:25,967 --> 00:30:27,933
<i>The seaman's coming today
to get his bike.</i>

581
00:30:28,067 --> 00:30:29,900
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE ROARS]

582
00:30:30,533 --> 00:30:31,867
- [LOUD CRASH]
- If you only knew....

583
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:34,700
...the things Gabo went through.

584
00:30:36,633 --> 00:30:39,333
- [KICK LANDS]
<i> - What did he do this time?</i>

585
00:30:40,067 --> 00:30:41,300
<i> Don't be like Gabo.</i>

586
00:30:41,467 --> 00:30:44,167
He's actually a good influence.
That's why we're following him.

587
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:46,167
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

588
00:30:47,567 --> 00:30:49,200
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]
